# shadcn-only UI

Frontend apps (`admin/` now, `client/` later) build interface controls from shadcn components in `components/ui`. Icons come from `lucide-react` only. Tailwind utilities are for layout and spacing.

Do not add another UI kit, and do not hand-roll controls shadcn already provides.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — second library, or a custom button
import { Button } from "@mui/material";
<button className="rounded bg-blue-500 px-4">Save</button>

// ✅ GOOD
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
<Button type="submit">Save</Button>
```

- Allowed kits: none besides shadcn. That includes MUI, Chakra, Ant Design, Bootstrap, and Headless UI.
- Do not hand-roll buttons, inputs, selects, dialogs, tables, badges, switches, or tabs.
- Radix is allowed only inside the generated files in `components/ui`.
- Compose pages from those primitives. App-specific layout (sidebar groups, page sections) stays outside `components/ui`.
- The future Express API is not a UI surface. This rule does not apply to server code.
